uld often go fishing  and the spectacular sunrises where the  light danced across the water  where invaluable quality time to lesion  that he always cherished  unfortunately the long-term  repercussions of working around such  dangerous substances  was evident and he witnessed a lot of  the devastating lasting effects  on his fellow he grew up to have immense  respect for hazardous materials  and a deep understanding for their  effects on the human body  [Music]  in a way to provide extra income for his  family he decided to volunteer in the  yunnan and gangshi provinces  helping to clear minds it was there that  he gained the attention of the hong kong  police department  as they saw his bravery and his ability  with disarming the dangerous weapons  from there he took the opportunity  afforded to him and joined with the  explosive ordnance disposal bureau  or eod the specialized unit within the  police department  is responsible for dealing with all  illegal explosive objects  including chemical biological  radiological  and nuclear weapons in hong kong the  bureau is trained  and equipped to deal with items both on  dry land and underwater  and is called out on average over one to  two times per week  the items they deal with range from  illegal fireworks and homemade bombs  to large world war ii aircraft bombs  working with the aod gave legion the  opportunity for on-site training  so he could continue to further  specialise in chemistry and  forensic-based education  lesions knowledge with nuclear radiation  along with his expertise  in biological and chemical substances  enabled him to later join hong kong's  special duties unit  and it was there that he teamed up with  ses operators smoke  and thatcher on his first ever joint  operation  in 2017 he was officially recruited into  rainbow  his past expertise in hong kong's cbrn  made him the obvious choice during the  formation of rainbow's own cbrn threat  unit  in 2018. over the years he continues to  consult 